diagnostics/nested-function-before-declaration.em:24:15: `z` is declared below `peek`
          print(z)
                ^
A nested function can use only the variables declared above it, as a block can. Move the declaration of `z` above `func peek`.
diagnostics/nested-function-before-declaration.em:37:10: `name` is already declared
      func name() {
           ^^^^
A function and a variable in one function cannot share a name. Choose a different name for one of them.
